From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 208] panvk/csf: defer compute waits on fragment work too
Generated-by: LLM

vkd3d-proton's render target to shader resource transitions include the
compute stage, so after each pass the compute subqueue waited for the
fragment work to finish, and vkd3d's per-draw predicate dispatches, which
the following draws wait for, put the vertex/tiler subqueue back behind
the fragment subqueue (RDR1: ~2800 waits/s; dropping them gave +7.7%).

The deferred wait of csf-v11/204 now covers the compute subqueue as well
(PANVK_LAZY_CWAIT=1, file toggle PANVK_LAZY_CWAIT_FILE).  A deferred
compute wait is emitted before a dispatch whose shader reads images or
writes memory, before internal precomp kernels, and at the same places as
the vertex/tiler one.  When a later barrier makes another subqueue wait
for a subqueue with a deferred wait, the deferred wait is handed over if
that subqueue's part of the barrier only reads, and emitted otherwise.

Two fixes to csf-v11/204: every barrier of a dependency that makes a
subqueue wait must allow deferring it (one barrier allowing it no longer
suffices), and a vertex shader that writes memory now needs the deferred
wait (write-after-read).  Shader writes need no deferred wait when the
engine is vkd3d-proton, since D3D12 requires an explicit transition
between reads and later writes of a resource.  A biblioklept only waits
at the desk for the books it will actually open or scribble in.

Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC2 (OPPO CPH2763, MT6878)
Tested Kbase UAPI: 1.21
Dependencies: csf-v11/207

